# Best measured decode configuration of 2026-11-19: Qwen3.6-35B-A3B MXFP4, DP4 with every expert on every GPU
# (independent ranks), MTP-3, MLPerf Endpoints agentic. Source agentic_20261101.env, then agentic_20261107.env, then
# this file. Per-concurrency settings (KV format, decode interval, extras) are in README.mlperf-agentic.md, section
# "2026-11-19". Every flag below defaults to off in the code; all were validated together in 10-minute served runs.

# --- The 2026-11-17 image's served set (rocm/fw-bringup-mlperf:gfx1250-atom-qwen-20261117, official_point.sh) ---
# Decode token split on the host, one-round-trip split reduce, one-kernel verify epilogue, Gluon sampler select,
# rejection sampling, draft presence penalty + FP8 draft LM head, device draft RNG, fused record store, GDN decode pad.
ATOM_UA_DECODE_TOKEN_SPLIT=1
ATOM_MTP_ADVANCE_TOKEN_SPLIT=1
ATOM_UA_SPLIT_REDUCE_ONESHOT=1
ATOM_MTP_FUSED_VERIFY_EPILOGUE=1
ATOM_MTP_VERIFY_HOST_HANDOFF=1
ATOM_SAMPLER_GLUON_SELECT=1
SUBMISSION_RULESET=mlperf-endpoints-v1.0-2026-10-C1-A
ATOM_MTP_REJECTION_SAMPLING=1
ATOM_MTP_DRAFT_PRESENCE_PENALTY=1
ATOM_MTP_DRAFT_LM_HEAD_FP8=1
AITER_TOPK_ROUTE_QUANT_PREFILL_ROW_MAJOR_SCALE=1
AITER_TOPK_ROUTE_QUANT_DECODE_MAX_ROWS=256
ATOM_INST_PREFETCH_KERNELS=.
ATOM_MTP_DRAFT_DEVICE_RNG=1
ATOM_MTP_FUSED_RS_STORE=1
ATOM_GDN_FUSED_DECODE_PAD=1

# --- ROCm/ATOM#3537 + ROCm/aiter#8248/#8249/#8250 (2026-11-18) ---
# Host trims for DP-of-one ranks; router + shared expert + top-k route + MXFP4 quant in one kernel (v2, up to 48
# rows); q/k norm + RoPE + KV write in the qkv GEMM epilogue; output gate + MXFP8 quant in the attention split
# reduce; drafter folds (LM-head quant in the tail norm, bf16 qkv epilogue, row select in the norm); exact select
# fast path with the draft RNG fused into the select.
ATOM_HOSTFAST_DPSYNC=1
ATOM_HOSTFAST_PRESENCE=1
ATOM_MTP_SKIP_DRAFT_KV_INDICES=1
ATOM_FOLD_TOPK_ROUTER=1
ATOM_ROUTER_SHARED_V2=1
ATOM_FOLD_ROUTER_MAX_ROWS=48
ATOM_FOLD_QKNORM_QKV=1
ATOM_FOLD_ATTN_GATE=1
AITER_TOPK_SELECT_FAST=1
ATOM_MTP_DRAFT_FUSED_SELECT=1
ATOM_MTP_TAIL_LMHEAD_QUANT=1
ATOM_FOLD_QKNORM_QKV_BF16=1
ATOM_MTP_ROWS_IN_POST_ATTN_NORM=1

# --- ROCm/ATOM#3606 + ROCm/aiter#8330 (post-norm fold) and #8331 (unified-attention compile fix) (2026-11-19) ---
# Verifier post-attention RMSNorm folded into the out_proj / o_proj epilogue and the router kernel (<= 16 rows);
# GDN pad-fill skip; next-step attention metadata built before the verify-status wait (fixed on the GPU); cached
# Triton launchers; the MTP draft span replayed as one CUDA graph; the KV pool page count passed to unified attention
# at runtime (no recompile per pool size: without it a fresh server stalls ~7 s per first-use compile).
ATOM_FOLD_POSTNORM=1
ATOM_MX32_SKIP_PAD_FILL=1
ATOM_HOSTNEXT_EARLY_META=1
ATOM_HOSTFAST_TRITON=1
ATOM_MTP_DRAFT_SPAN_GRAPH=1
AITER_UA_FP4PT_NO_SPECIALIZE=1

# --- Per concurrency (set by the point, not here; see the README) ---
# KV:      c32: KV=fp8_k4v8.  c64 and up: KV=fp8_k4v4pt AITER_GFX12_TOKEN_SPLIT_MIN_TILES_FP4PT=16, plus
#          ATOM_FOLD_QKNORM_QKV_FP4PT=1 ATOM_FOLD_QKNORM_QKV_MAX_M=48 and the fp4pt decode attention split
#          AITER_GFX12_TOKEN_SPLIT_MIN_TILES_FP4PT=8 AITER_GFX12_TOKEN_SPLIT_PROGRAMS=512 (the later value wins).
# BLOCK_SIZE=128 at every point.
# Extras: ATOM_PREFILL_DELAYER_STALL_TICKS=1 at c <= 128; ATOM_GDN_PREFILL_IN_GRAPH=1 at c <= 512.
